description: Never add a Cursor or LLM signature to git commits or GitHub pushes
alwaysApply: true
---

# No Cursor / LLM git signature

Commits and pushes from this repo must look like a normal human git commit.

Do **not** add any Cursor, Copilot, Claude, or other LLM tag, trailer, footer, or co-author.

Forbidden (any casing / spacing):

- `Made with Cursor`
- `Made-with: Cursor`
- `Generated by Cursor`
- `Co-authored-by: ...Cursor...`
- `Co-authored-by: ...noreply.github.com` for a bot unless the user asked
- 🤖 / "via Cursor" / agent IDs in the subject or body

```text
# BAD
Add cook skip for unchanged init.

Made with Cursor
```

```text
# GOOD
Add cook skip for unchanged init.

Skip the EE recook when hourly and synoptic inits match the manifest.
```

Use only the commit message the user wants (or a short why). No trailers. Do not pass `--trailer` for Cursor.

`.githooks/commit-msg` (installed as `.git/hooks/commit-msg`) strips these lines if Cursor injects them after you write the message. Do not delete or skip that hook.
